      "role": "user",
      "content": "so basically you're saying that the 'fairness' side of things just outweighs the pure math/accuracy side. if we're being honest, isn't it technically a flawed model if we're intentionally deviating from the most accurate risk prediction just to hit these social targets? wouldn't that eventually be seen as social engineering rather than actual engineering?",
